{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Infinite queries are for lists that load more data into one cache entry. Use "},{"type":"link","href":"../reference/functions/createInfiniteQueryController.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createInfiniteQueryController"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"An infinite query result contains:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"data.pages"},{"type":"text","value":": fetched pages"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"data.pageParams"},{"type":"text","value":": page parameters used for those pages"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fetchNextPage"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fetchPreviousPage"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"hasNextPage"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"hasPreviousPage"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isFetchingNextPage"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isFetchingPreviousPage"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"load-more-example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Load More Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { LitElement, html } from 'lit'\nimport { createInfiniteQueryController } from '@tanstack/lit-query'\n\nclass ProjectsList extends LitElement {\n  private readonly projects = createInfiniteQueryController(this, {\n    queryKey: ['projects'],\n    queryFn: ({ pageParam }) => fetchProjectsPage(pageParam),\n    initialPageParam: 1,\n    getNextPageParam: (lastPage) =>\n      lastPage.hasMore ? lastPage.page + 1 : undefined,\n  })\n\n  render() {\n    const query = this.projects()\n\n    if (query.isPending) return html`Loading...`\n    if (query.isError) return html`Error: ${query.error.message}`\n\n    return html`\n      ${query.data.pages.map(\n        (page) => html`\n          ${page.projects.map((project) => html`<p>${project.name}</p>`)}\n        `,\n      )}\n\n      <button\n        ?disabled=${!query.hasNextPage || query.isFetching}\n        @click=${() => this.projects.fetchNextPage()}\n      >\n        ${\n          query.isFetchingNextPage\n            ? 'Loading more...'\n            : query.hasNextPage\n              ? 'Load More'\n              : 'Nothing more to load'\n        }\n      </button>\n    `\n  }\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"page-parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Page Parameters"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"initialPageParam"},{"type":"text","value":" is required. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getNextPageParam"},{"type":"text","value":" decides whether another page exists and what value should be passed as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pageParam"},{"type":"text","value":" to the next query function call."}]},{"type":"code","value":"createInfiniteQueryController(this, {\n  queryKey: ['projects'],\n  queryFn: ({ pageParam }) => fetchProjectsPage(pageParam),\n  initialPageParam: 1,\n  getNextPageParam: (lastPage) =>\n    lastPage.hasMore ? lastPage.page + 1 : undefined,\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returning "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"undefined"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"null"},{"type":"text","value":" means there is no next page."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"avoid-overlapping-fetches","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Avoid Overlapping Fetches"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"There is one ongoing fetch for an infinite query cache entry. If you call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fetchNextPage"},{"type":"text","value":" while a background refetch is running, you can overwrite data. Disable the button or check "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"!query.isFetching"},{"type":"text","value":" before loading more:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"if (query.hasNextPage && !query.isFetching) {\n  this.projects.fetchNextPage()\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"paginated-alternative","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Paginated Alternative"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If your UI shows one page at a time, a normal query with a page in the key can be a better fit. The "},{"type":"link","href":"../examples/pagination","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pagination example"}]},{"type":"text","value":" uses "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createQueryController"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"placeholderData: keepPreviousData"},{"type":"text","value":", prefetching, and mutations to demonstrate that pattern."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"load-more-example","text":"Load More Example","level":2},{"id":"page-parameters","text":"Page Parameters","level":2},{"id":"avoid-overlapping-fetches","text":"Avoid Overlapping Fetches","level":2},{"id":"paginated-alternative","text":"Paginated Alternative","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nInfinite queries are for lists that load more data into one cache entry. Use [`createInfiniteQueryController`](../reference/functions/createInfiniteQueryController.md).\n\nAn infinite query result contains:\n\n- `data.pages`: fetched pages\n- `data.pageParams`: page parameters used for those pages\n- `fetchNextPage` and `fetchPreviousPage`\n- `hasNextPage` and `hasPreviousPage`\n- `isFetchingNextPage` and `isFetchingPreviousPage`\n\n## Load More Example\n\n```ts\nimport { LitElement, html } from 'lit'\nimport { createInfiniteQueryController } from '@tanstack/lit-query'\n\nclass ProjectsList extends LitElement {\n  private readonly projects = createInfiniteQueryController(this, {\n    queryKey: ['projects'],\n    queryFn: ({ pageParam }) => fetchProjectsPage(pageParam),\n    initialPageParam: 1,\n    getNextPageParam: (lastPage) =>\n      lastPage.hasMore ? lastPage.page + 1 : undefined,\n  })\n\n  render() {\n    const query = this.projects()\n\n    if (query.isPending) return html`Loading...`\n    if (query.isError) return html`Error: ${query.error.message}`\n\n    return html`\n      ${query.data.pages.map(\n        (page) => html`\n          ${page.projects.map((project) => html`<p>${project.name}</p>`)}\n        `,\n      )}\n\n      <button\n        ?disabled=${!query.hasNextPage || query.isFetching}\n        @click=${() => this.projects.fetchNextPage()}\n      >\n        ${\n          query.isFetchingNextPage\n            ? 'Loading more...'\n            : query.hasNextPage\n              ? 'Load More'\n              : 'Nothing more to load'\n        }\n      </button>\n    `\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Page Parameters\n\n`initialPageParam` is required. `getNextPageParam` decides whether another page exists and what value should be passed as `pageParam` to the next query function call.\n\n```ts\ncreateInfiniteQueryController(this, {\n  queryKey: ['projects'],\n  queryFn: ({ pageParam }) => fetchProjectsPage(pageParam),\n  initialPageParam: 1,\n  getNextPageParam: (lastPage) =>\n    lastPage.hasMore ? lastPage.page + 1 : undefined,\n})\n```\n\nReturning `undefined` or `null` means there is no next page.\n\n## Avoid Overlapping Fetches\n\nThere is one ongoing fetch for an infinite query cache entry. If you call `fetchNextPage` while a background refetch is running, you can overwrite data. Disable the button or check `!query.isFetching` before loading more:\n\n```ts\nif (query.hasNextPage && !query.isFetching) {\n  this.projects.fetchNextPage()\n}\n```\n\n## Paginated Alternative\n\nIf your UI shows one page at a time, a normal query with a page in the key can be a better fit. The [Pagination example](../examples/pagination) uses `createQueryController`, `placeholderData: keepPreviousData`, prefetching, and mutations to demonstrate that pattern.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: infinite-queries\ntitle: Infinite Queries\n---\n\nInfinite queries are for lists that load more data into one cache entry. Use [`createInfiniteQueryController`](../reference/functions/createInfiniteQueryController.md).\n\nAn infinite query result contains:\n\n- `data.pages`: fetched pages\n- `data.pageParams`: page parameters used for those pages\n- `fetchNextPage` and `fetchPreviousPage`\n- `hasNextPage` and `hasPreviousPage`\n- `isFetchingNextPage` and `isFetchingPreviousPage`\n\n## Load More Example\n\n```ts\nimport { LitElement, html } from 'lit'\nimport { createInfiniteQueryController } from '@tanstack/lit-query'\n\nclass ProjectsList extends LitElement {\n  private readonly projects = createInfiniteQueryController(this, {\n    queryKey: ['projects'],\n    queryFn: ({ pageParam }) => fetchProjectsPage(pageParam),\n    initialPageParam: 1,\n    getNextPageParam: (lastPage) =>\n      lastPage.hasMore ? lastPage.page + 1 : undefined,\n  })\n\n  render() {\n    const query = this.projects()\n\n    if (query.isPending) return html`Loading...`\n    if (query.isError) return html`Error: ${query.error.message}`\n\n    return html`\n      ${query.data.pages.map(\n        (page) => html`\n          ${page.projects.map((project) => html`<p>${project.name}</p>`)}\n        `,\n      )}\n\n      <button\n        ?disabled=${!query.hasNextPage || query.isFetching}\n        @click=${() => this.projects.fetchNextPage()}\n      >\n        ${\n          query.isFetchingNextPage\n            ? 'Loading more...'\n            : query.hasNextPage\n              ? 'Load More'\n              : 'Nothing more to load'\n        }\n      </button>\n    `\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Page Parameters\n\n`initialPageParam` is required. `getNextPageParam` decides whether another page exists and what value should be passed as `pageParam` to the next query function call.\n\n```ts\ncreateInfiniteQueryController(this, {\n  queryKey: ['projects'],\n  queryFn: ({ pageParam }) => fetchProjectsPage(pageParam),\n  initialPageParam: 1,\n  getNextPageParam: (lastPage) =>\n    lastPage.hasMore ? lastPage.page + 1 : undefined,\n})\n```\n\nReturning `undefined` or `null` means there is no next page.\n\n## Avoid Overlapping Fetches\n\nThere is one ongoing fetch for an infinite query cache entry. If you call `fetchNextPage` while a background refetch is running, you can overwrite data. Disable the button or check `!query.isFetching` before loading more:\n\n```ts\nif (query.hasNextPage && !query.isFetching) {\n  this.projects.fetchNextPage()\n}\n```\n\n## Paginated Alternative\n\nIf your UI shows one page at a time, a normal query with a page in the key can be a better fit. The [Pagination example](../examples/pagination) uses `createQueryController`, `placeholderData: keepPreviousData`, prefetching, and mutations to demonstrate that pattern.\n"}
